"Hollow Tarn became a tidepool this winter: the Horizon under it is thin and thinning."
"The drowned shrine under the tarn is a temple of the same ancient make as the ruins by the Vale."
"The shrine's steps go down forty feet of water to a door into three dry, air-filled chambers."
"The Vestige broke through the Horizon in the shrine's lowest chamber on the longest night."
"The Vestige left a crust of gold, like cooled metal, on the lowest chamber's floor stones."
"In the lowest chamber a shaft of still water goes down past any light: a way to the Sea itself."
"The shrine's lintel is carved with the old words, which Eidhrin cannot pass."
"Aberrants off the Whitecombs are drawn to the tarn by its thinning Horizon, as moths to a lamp."
"Deep Children climb the shrine steps on moonless nights and sing from the shallows."
"The Deep Children of the tarn are pale, eyeless, child-sized things that sing people into the water."
"Cold iron burns a Deep Child like a brand, and they will not cross a line of it."
"The Deep Children sang Liss Aske into the tarn after she took off her cold iron."
"If the tarn's Horizon breaks wholly, a true Aberrant will come up out of it into the valley."
"At the pace it thins, the tarn's Horizon breaks wholly by midsummer."
"A Talent of Second Depth or more who draws deep beside the tarn feels the Sea pulling at them."
